# Plot types: GRAY / CONTOUR / WIRE / SLICE / ROW on the /null device; TEXT / BINARY / MAT
# / FITS write an OPD file beside the DECK (hence the COPY) (cmdref: Outputs, plot types)
# Each selector prints 'Plot type set to X'; the file types name the file they write.
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/Cassegrain.in
old $DECK
gray
opd 3
/null
contour
opd 3
wire
opd 3
slice
opd 3
text
opd 3
binary
opd 3
mat
opd 3
fits
opd 3
! ls -1 $TMP
# EXPECT: Plot type set to GRAY
# EXPECT: Plot type set to CONTOUR
# EXPECT: Plot type set to WIRE
# EXPECT: Plot type set to SLICE
# EXPECT: Plot type set to TEXT
# EXPECT: Plot type set to BINARY
# EXPECT: Plot type set to MAT
# EXPECT: Plot type set to FITS
# EXPECT: (RMS OPD error is\s+1\.5453\d+D-02[\s\S]*){8}
# EXPECT: Cassegrain\.in\.OPD3\.txt
# EXPECT: Cassegrain\.in\.OPD3\.fit
# EXPECT: MAT output is not built into this macos
# EXPECT-NOT: Unknown plot type
# EXPECT-NOT: too long for FITS
# (pre-fix: MAT printed 'Unknown plot type iPloTyp = 9'; FITS refused any deck path longer
#  than 18 characters for its FILENAME card after announcing the file, and cut the output
#  path at 40 characters)
